# The build context of services/dispat/Dockerfile alone. BuildKit reads a
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the one at the repository root, so
# this widens the context for this build without touching the root file, whose
# deny-all keeps the four image contexts down to install.sh.
#
# Nested re-inclusion needs every level spelled out: an exception cannot reach
# into a folder the line above excluded, so services/ is let back in before its
# children are filtered.
*
!pkg
!services
services/*
!services/dispat

# The smoke suite the test stage runs against the built binaries; see the
# Dockerfile's test stage.
!tests

# The install manifest the tiny-toolchain stage runs, and nothing else under
# scripts/: it is the one file that carries the TinyGo fork's pin, and letting
# the whole folder in would put every unrelated script's edits in this build's
# cache key. The same spelling out of every level as above: scripts/ is let
# back in, then filtered down to the one file.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/install-tools.sh

# The export folder of a previous build. It is the one thing under
# services/dispat that is output rather than source, and shipping it into the
# context would grow with every build.
services/dispat/dist
